    <bpmn:process id="W_W1806" name="W1806. Rebate Analytics &amp; Margin Impact Dashboard" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly analytics cycle
Frequency: Monthly dashboard; weekly during peak promotional periods
Volume: Continuous analytics
Owner: FP&amp;A
Participants: FP&amp;A, VP Merchandising, Category Managers, CFO
Source: workflow W1806 — Rebate Analytics &amp; Margin Impact Dashboard</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1806_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1806_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1806_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1806_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1806_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1806_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1806_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1806_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1806_Start4" name="Monthly analytics cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1806_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1806_Task5" name="Monthly rebate analytics dashboard: (a) total rebate income (accrued) by month…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly rebate analytics dashboard: (a) total rebate income (accrued) by month, quarter, YTD, (b) rebate as % of COGS (effective gross margin improvement), (c) rebate by category and vendor, (d) rebate claim success rate (% claimed vs. % received), (e) co-op marketing income and utilization, (f) markdown allowances recovered from vendors, (g) new store opening rebates collected, (h) rebate income vs. budget, (i) top 20 vendors by rebate income, (j) vendors with declining rebate income (risk of loss)
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1806_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1806_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1806_Task6" name="Margin impact analysis: (a) gross margin before rebates vs. gross margin after…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Margin impact analysis: (a) gross margin before rebates vs. gross margin after rebates by category, (b) rebate income contribution to EBITDA, (c) effective vendor margin improvement by category, (d) promotional margin impact (rebate + co-op − markdown cost = net promotional margin)
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1806_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1806_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1806_Task7" name="CFO uses rebate analytics in Board reporting: (a) rebate income as % of revenue…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CFO uses rebate analytics in Board reporting: (a) rebate income as % of revenue (benchmark: 2–4% of COGS for large retailers), (b) trend analysis: is BuildRight capturing all available vendor incentives? (c) comparison to industry benchmarks
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): Board
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1806_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1806_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1806_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1806_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1806_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-360 (ensure controlled execution — Rebate Settlement &amp; Analytics (PA-39.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: FP&amp;A</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
