    <bpmn:process id="W_W1810" name="W1810. Rebate Process Automation &amp; System Enhancement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual process improvement cycle; internal audit recommendation
Frequency: Continuous improvement
Volume: Ongoing
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, IT, AP Manager, CIO
Source: workflow W1810 — Rebate Process Automation &amp; System Enhancement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1810_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1810_Lane1" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1810_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1810_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1810_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1810_Lane2" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1810_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1810_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1810_Start4" name="Annual process improvement cycle; internal audit recommendation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1810_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1810_Task5" name="Identify automation opportunities: (a) auto-accrual: system calculates rebate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Identify automation opportunities: (a) auto-accrual: system calculates rebate accrual directly from purchase data without manual intervention (currently semi-automated; target: fully automated for standard agreements), (b) auto-claim generation: system generates rebate claim worksheets automatically at period end, (c) vendor portal integration: claims submitted electronically via vendor portal with auto-populated data, (d) settlement matching: auto-match vendor credit notes to claims using AI/ML pattern matching, (e) alerts: automatic notification when vendor crosses volume threshold, when claim is overdue, when accrual rate changes
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1810_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1810_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1810_Task6" name="Prioritize automation based on: (a) volume of manual effort saved (high…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Prioritize automation based on: (a) volume of manual effort saved (high: auto-accrual for 200 agreements), (b) error reduction (high: manual calculation errors on tier thresholds), (c) margin leakage prevention (high: missed claims due to manual process gaps), (d) implementation complexity (medium: vendor portal integration requires vendor cooperation)
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / CIO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1810_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1810_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1810_Task7" name="Implement in phases: (a) Phase 1: auto-accrual and auto-claim generation (3–6…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Implement in phases: (a) Phase 1: auto-accrual and auto-claim generation (3–6 months), (b) Phase 2: vendor portal integration for claim submission (6–12 months), (c) Phase 3: AI-powered settlement matching and anomaly detection (12–18 months)
Responsible (R): IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 18 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1810_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1810_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1810_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1810_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1810_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-360 (ensure controlled execution — Rebate Settlement &amp; Analytics (PA-39.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
